{"timestamp": 1779431013.6778705, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 13, "data": {"caller": "player_0", "reason": "Alice reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Bob"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779431013.6788042, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 13, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779431025.4932976, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I just found Bob's body in Medbay! Frank, you were standing right there in the room with the body when I walked in and reported it, what exactly happened? \n\nFor my route, I went Storage -> Lower Engine -> Upper Engine -> Medbay. \n\nHere is a crucial piece of information: when I was in Upper Engine, I saw Eve walk in *from* the direction of Medbay around tick 9. \n\nSo the killer is almost certainly either Frank (who was on the body when I found it) or Eve (who was seen leaving the scene of the crime shortly before). Frank, Eve, we need to hear your defenses right now. Everyone else, listen closely to what they say."}}
{"timestamp": 1779431050.2502124, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I didn\u2019t kill Bob. My route was O2 -> Upper Engine -> back through O2 -> Cafeteria -> Medbay -> Electrical -> Medbay. I saw Charlie early in O2, then later I saw Bob in Medbay around tick 11.\n\nI stepped into Electrical briefly and came back into Medbay, and Alice reported basically right after. From my view, I wasn\u2019t camping a body \u2014 I had just returned and Alice came in from the left side.\n\nAlice saying she saw Eve leaving from Medbay direction around tick 9 is important, but if Bob was alive when I saw him later, then either Eve came back, Alice\u2019s timing is off, or someone else came through after. I want to hear Eve\u2019s exact route. Also Alice, how long were you in Upper Engine before coming into Medbay?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779431064.5069253, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Listen up! I have very important timeline information that clears Eve from Alice's suspicion and narrows this down to either Frank or Alice. \n\nMy route was Electrical -> Medbay -> Storage. The crucial detail here is that I saw Bob alive down in Storage at ticks 7 and 8. \n\nSince it takes 2 ticks to travel from Storage up to Medbay, Bob could not have possibly arrived in Medbay until tick 10 at the absolute earliest. Alice, you said you saw Eve leaving Medbay around tick 9. Even if that's true, Eve couldn't have killed Bob, because Bob wasn't even in Medbay yet! \n\nFurthermore, Frank's claim that he saw Bob alive in Medbay around tick 11 lines up perfectly with my sighting. Bob must have walked from Storage to Medbay right after I saw him. \n\nThis means the murder happened between tick 11 and tick 13. Frank, you admit you were in Medbay around that exact time. Alice, you walked into Medbay right at the end to report it. The killer is almost certainly one of you two. Eve, Charlie, we need to hear from you. For now, I'm keeping my eye on Alice and Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779431081.9329562, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Diana is completely right, and her timeline clears me perfectly. To confirm Alice's sighting: yes, my route was Cafeteria -> Electrical -> Medbay -> Upper Engine. I walked into Upper Engine at tick 9 and saw Alice there. We were in Upper Engine together for ticks 9 and 10. \n\nHere is the absolute nail in Frank's coffin: I saw Alice leave Upper Engine heading towards Medbay exactly at tick 11. It takes exactly 2 ticks to walk from Upper Engine to Medbay, meaning Alice arrived at tick 13 and immediately reported the body.\n\nNow look at Frank's defense. Frank claims he was in Medbay at tick 11, \"stepped into Electrical briefly,\" and came back just as Alice walked in. Frank, that is geographically impossible. Medbay to Electrical is a 2-tick walk each way, making it a 4-tick round trip. If you were in Medbay at tick 11 and left for Electrical, you wouldn't be back until tick 15! \n\nYou couldn't have gone to Electrical and back before Alice walked in at tick 13. You were standing on Bob's body at tick 13 because you never left Medbay. You killed him right after Diana saw him, and Alice walked in and caught you red-handed. \n\nWe are voting Frank. Charlie, you have the last word, but the math proves Frank is lying."}}
{"timestamp": 1779431097.4532914, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I can confirm the very beginning of Frank's route. I was in Oxygen and saw Frank walk in from Upper Engine around tick 5. \n\nHowever, that's where my defense of Frank ends, because Eve is absolutely spot-on with the math. Let's look at the facts:\n\n1. Diana confirms Bob was alive in Storage at tick 8, meaning he couldn't reach Medbay until tick 10 at the earliest.\n2. Frank admits he was in Medbay with Bob around tick 11. \n3. Alice left Upper Engine at tick 11 and arrived in Medbay at tick 13 to report the body.\n4. The corridor from Medbay to Electrical takes 2 ticks. \n\nFrank, if you were in Medbay at tick 11, went to Electrical, and came back, that is a minimum 4-tick round trip. You would not have been back in Medbay until tick 15. The fact that Alice caught you in Medbay at tick 13 proves you never left. You stayed in Medbay and killed Bob right after he walked up from Storage. \n\nGreat logic from Diana and Eve. The timeline is air-tight and catches Frank in a blatant lie about his movements. I'm voting Frank. Let's get him out of here."}}
